; The people. The ones with wander= walk about that many tiles round where they're put. The ones with
; a cast= have conversations, and a yellow mark when one's a job.
;
; The terrace and the temple steps.
npc oswin 40.5 18.5 cast=oswin facing=down say="Touch nothing, climb nothing, pick no flowers.|The King walks the terrace at dusk.|Move along, kindly."
npc courtier 47 19 look=160 name="A Courtier" facing=down wander=3 say="One does not simply walk onto the terrace. Oh. You did.|Lord Chancellor Crane hosts a supper tonight. You're not invited.|The Princess missed council again. Riding, apparently."
npc gardener 27.5 18.5 look=467 name="The Palace Gardener" wander=3 say="Mind the roses. They're older than you.|Thirty years I've clipped these hedges. They still argue.|The King likes the pink ones. He says they look surprised."
npc hesper 18 18.5 cast=hesper facing=down say="The door's open to all.|Muddy boots are welcome. Mostly.|The bells will ring at dusk, if the boy remembers."
npc pilgrim 22 19 name="A Pilgrim" sheet=pilgrim facing=down say="Listen for the temple bells at dusk.|I walked from the river farms to pray here.|The bells were sweeter last year, they tell me."
npc acolyte-a 13 19 look=192 name="An Acolyte" facing=down say="Sun's blessing on you, traveller.|The bells ring at dusk. Probably. Mostly.|Mind the steps. Sister Hesper just swept them."
npc acolyte-b 14.5 19.5 look=230 name="An Acolyte" facing=down say="The temple's open to all. Even the muddy.|We pray for the soldiers sent east. Every morning.|Shh. The new bellringer is practising. Badly."
npc courier 49 20.5 name="A Courier" sheet=courier facing=right say="Letters for the guildhall. Mind out.|Three for the guildhall, one for the Spire, none for me.|If I'm late again, I'm a fisherman."
npc ilsa 64.5 19 cast=ilsa facing=down wander=2 say="Don't jostle me, these are sealed. Well. Officially.|The Archmage is never wrong. Never.|Scrolls, scrolls, more scrolls."
npc guild-clerk 63 19.5 look=449 name="A Guild Clerk" facing=down say="Guild business only. Have you got guild business?|Masons, merchants and mages. The mages never fill in forms.|The Arcanum Spire sends a runner every hour lately."
npc maid 60 20 name="A Maid" sheet=maid facing=down wander=4 say="The guildhall's busy today.|Mages tracking ash on my clean floors again.|Polish, sweep, polish. Then the mages come back."

; The plaza: the elder, Lark and her critic, the Watch by the east statue, the old couple at the bench.
npc elder 39 32 name="The Elder" sheet=elder facing=down say="Welcome to Questeria. Mind the road past the gate.|Forty years I've watched this fountain. It still surprises me.|The Lantern Market's east. Follow the smell of bread."
npc old-man 46 31 name="An Old Man" sheet=old-man facing=left wander=3 say="The fountain's older than the palace. So they say.|My knees say rain by Thursday.|In my day we had one lantern and we shared it."
npc lark 34.8 23.5 cast=lark facing=right say="A verse for a copper, a chorus for two!|Ohh, the lanterns of the harbour...|Everybody's a critic. Mostly him."
npc heckler 36.8 23 look=446 name="A Heckler" facing=left say="Learn a new song!|Six times! She's sung that line six times!|I'm not heckling. I'm reviewing."
npc watch-a 54.5 24 cast=watch facing=right say="Keep it moving, citizens.|Double shift again. My feet have filed a complaint.|See a red bandana, tell the Watch."
npc watch-b 56 24.5 cast=watch facing=left say="Half the barracks is in Greywatch. The other half is me.|We're not stretched thin. We're see-through.|No running by the fountain. Captain's orders."
npc old-a 45.3 35.5 look=131 name="Old Bram" facing=down say="Forty years of peace. Forty.|In my day the fountain was a puddle with ambitions.|The King waved at me once. I waved back. We're friends now."
npc old-b 46.7 35.5 look=102 name="Old Edda" facing=down say="Don't mind Bram. He's grumbled since the coronation.|You've a kind face. Eat something.|Ash on the wind from the east, my sister writes. I don't like it."
npc tamsin 53.5 34.5 cast=tamsin facing=right say="Stay on the paths.|The Lodge is three rangers short.|If the birds go quiet, so do you."

; The west houses.
npc neighbour 9.5 32.5 look=403 name="A Neighbour" facing=down say="Mind my flower boxes, they're prize-winning.|Well. They will be. Next year.|Lovely day for it. Whatever it is you're doing."
npc weaver 16 34 name="The Weaver" sheet=weaver facing=down say="I spun the palace banners.|Navy and gold for the King. Pink and gold for the Princess.|Thread's dear this year. Everything's dear."
npc old-woman 8 37 name="An Old Woman" sheet=old-woman facing=right wander=3 say="Mind the canal. It's deeper than it looks.|My husband fell in on our wedding day. Still damp.|You've a look of the sea about you."

; The market: the lantern seller and the flower seller by the Flagon, Wren working the crowd, and in
; the square the keepers in front of their stalls, two of them gossiping over the fruit.
npc lantern-seller 60 29 look=437 name="A Lantern Seller" facing=down say="Lanterns! The market's named for them, you know.|Light one at dusk and the whole street glows.|Paper, glass or brass. Brass lasts. Paper's prettier."
npc trader 74 27 name="The Trader" sheet=trader facing=down say="Fresh from the coast. Fresh enough.|Everything's half price. Half of a higher price.|The east ships stopped coming. Don't ask me why."
npc gossip-a 79.2 27 look=464 name="A Cheesemonger" facing=right say="Cheese from the river farms! Smells worse than it tastes!|Chancellor Crane's got a new carriage. Gold wheels, if you please.|The Princess bought a wedge off me once. Paid double."
npc gossip-b 80.8 27 look=419 name="A Fruit Seller" facing=left say="Apples, pears, river plums!|Plums are late. The Mirewood farms say the bees went odd.|Don't squeeze the pears. They bruise like courtiers."
npc spice-seller 74 36.5 look=438 name="A Spice Seller" facing=down say="Pepper, saffron, ember-salt!|Ember-salt makes you sweat in a good way.|The eastern spice ships stopped coming. Prices doubled."
npc osric 80 36.5 cast=osric facing=down say="Silk from the south! Linen from the river farms!|Has anybody seen a green book? Brass corners?|Fifteen years. Fifteen years in that book."
npc seamstress 82.2 36.5 name="The Seamstress" sheet=seamstress facing=left say="Pink's in this year. It's always in.|The Princess wears riding leathers. Nobody can stop her.|Mind the pins. I count them."
npc wren 64.5 33.5 cast=wren wander=3 say="Spare a copper? No? Worth asking.|Nice belt. Very secure.|The Watch never looks down. I'm down here."
npc flower-seller 66.6 36.2 name="The Flower Seller" sheet=flower-seller facing=left say="From the palace gardens. Don't tell anyone.|Roses for love, lilies for sorry, daisies for I forgot.|The gardener and I have an understanding."
npc porter 77 31 name="A Porter" sheet=porter facing=right wander=4 say="Crates, barrels, crates. All day.|Lift with your legs, they say. My legs say no.|Mind your toes, this one's heavy."
npc smith 97.5 32 name="The Smith" sheet=smith facing=left say="Nothing to mend? Lucky you.|Half the Watch's blades went east with the Watch.|A good edge never asks where you're going."
npc farmhand 94 18 name="A Farmhand" sheet=farmhand facing=right wander=4 say="First time in the capital? Me too.|The river farms are too quiet, my da says.|Everything's so clean here. I keep wiping my boots."

; Along the canal, and south of it.
npc boatman 33.5 37 look=106 name="A Boatman" facing=down say="Canal ride? A copper to the harbour, two if you talk.|The canals run all the way down to the sea.|Don't lean over the side. The fish here are nosy."
npc kid-a 18 45.5 look=186 name="A Child" wander=5 say="You're it!|I'm a Hollowed! Grrr!|My dad says the east is all ash now.|Bet I can jump the canal. Bet you."
npc kid-b 20 46 look=144 name="A Child" wander=5 say="No fair, you always pick!|When I grow up I'm joining the Mages Guild.|Have you got a sword? Can I hold it? Please?"
npc youth 51 43 name="A Youth" sheet=youth facing=left wander=4 say="There's a barrow up the old road. Haunted, probably.|Dared my brother to go in. He came back very fast.|They say a king's buried in it. Or a cook. Somebody important."
npc washerwoman 88.3 45 look=411 name="A Washerwoman" facing=down say="Out the way, love, wet sheets coming through.|Palace linen. You'd think kings sweat gold.|Canal water's for washing, not drinking. Learned that the hard way."
npc child 85.5 49 name="A Child" sheet=child facing=left wander=5 say="Bet you can't catch me.|You're slow! Slower than my gran!|Are you an adventurer? Have you killed a dragon?"

; The avenue and the gate: Brisk of the Watch just inside it.
npc traveller 43 45 name="A Traveller" sheet=traveller facing=down say="Long road out there.|Bandits on the Mirewood road, they say.|Questeria's grand. Shame about the prices."
npc carter 34.8 53 look=409 name="A Carter" facing=right say="Wagon's empty. Bandits on the Mirewood road took the rest.|Took my cargo and charged me a toll for the privilege.|Brisk says he's got no men. He's got a dog, though."
npc brisk 49 53.5 cast=brisk facing=left say="Gate's open. Mind the road.|Two recruits and a dog. The dog's the best of us.|Highwaymen on the Mirewood road. Travel in pairs."
